    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d392">

                <pb facs="0872" n="862" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg862"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 12.</seg></opener>
                <head>Acting Consul Fullarton to Earl Russell.—(Received February 1, 1864.)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Savannah,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-10-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 23, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord:</hi> I have the honor to enclose to your
                    lordship a copy of my reply to Mr. Benjamin’s despatch to me of the 8th instant,
                    conveying the president’s order to depart promptly from the confederacy, and in
                    the mean time to cease the exercise of consular functions.</p>
                <p>Mr. Benjamin has thought proper to publish his despatch to me in the Richmond
                    newspapers.</p>
                <pb facs="0873" n="863" xml:id="pg863"/>
                <p>Having had committed to my charge the interests of several parties absent in
                    Europe, which my departure would seriously injure, I have requested Mr. Benjamin
                    to rescind that portion of the order requiring me actually to withdraw from the
                    confederacy.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. FULLARTON.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d392-a1.xml" xpointer="d392-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
